Stop the gateway log growing with every refusal too

Capping the policy audit log left the other half open. The gateway
logs each refusal to its own file as well, and that has no cap: the
same flood that filled 91KB of audit log filled 66KB of gateway.log
beside it, so a guest could still fill the host's disk, just slower.

The refusal is already recorded in the audit log, which is capped and
is what `sandbox policy log` reads. Logging it a second time only gave
the guest a second way to do it, so those lines are debug now. What
remains in gateway.log is what the gateway itself did, which the guest
does not control.

diff --git a/pkg/services/dns/dns.go b/pkg/services/dns/dns.go
index 810cffe..40449a8 100644
--- a/pkg/services/dns/dns.go
+++ b/pkg/services/dns/dns.go
@@ -132,7 +132,11 @@ func (h *dnsHandler) addAnswers(m *dns.Msg) {
 		// very likely exists, we are declining to look it up.
 		if h.policy != nil {
 			if v := h.policy.AllowName(q.Name); !v.Allowed {
-				log.Infof("policy: refused dns %s (%s)", q.Name, v.Reason)
+				// Debug, not Info: the guest decides how many refusals there are, and this
+				// file has no cap. The refusal is already recorded in the policy audit log,
+				// which is capped and is what `sandbox policy log` reads -- so logging it here
+				// as well only gave a guest a second way to fill the host's disk.
+				log.Debugf("policy: refused dns %s (%s)", q.Name, v.Reason)
 				// Record it: a name that was never allowed is the commonest
 				// refusal, and without this the audit log is silent about it.
 				h.policy.RecordName(q.Name, v)
